      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards do you reference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling references NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 guidelines for media sanitization that require verification of purge-level overwrite or physical destruction. Under HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312 requirements, electronic protected health information on disposed devices must be rendered irretrievable. STS provides processes designed to support these standards along with accurate reporting and chain of custody documentation for audit readiness across Kern County healthcare, energy, and government clients. “NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 requires that sanitization render data recovery infeasible,” the standard that guides our verified destruction methods. Our 200,000 sq ft processing operation has supported compliance needs for organizations since 2011. Equipment collected in Bakersfield is transported to certified facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas for final processing and material recovery. This approach delivers the transparent, documented service Bakersfield organizations in regulated industries require."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We serve Bakersfield, Kern County, and surrounding San Joaquin Valley communities including energy corridors, agricultural operations near major freight routes, and logistics hubs. Complimentary pickup is available for qualifying volumes from energy sites, large-scale farming operations, hospitals, school districts and municipal facilities. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me in Bakersfield and Kern County find STS provides scheduled pickup with full documentation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is complimentary for qualifying volumes. Contact us to determine eligibility based on your specific equipment mix and location within the Bakersfield service area. Most agricultural, energy, healthcare and education clients in Kern County qualify for no-cost scheduled pickup with same-week availability."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you handle data security?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS provides processes that support NIST 800-88 guidelines for data sanitization. Accurate reporting and chain of custody documentation are provided with every project so clients maintain audit-ready records. Under California regulations classifying electronics as universal waste, our services help organizations meet DTSC and CalRecycle requirements while protecting sensitive information from energy operators, healthcare networks, school districts and government agencies throughout Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer on-site data destruction in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS offers scheduled on-site hard drive shredding and witnessed destruction options for Bakersfield clients with strict security requirements. For most projects equipment is securely transported to our certified processing facilities where NIST 800-88 compliant destruction occurs under chain of custody documentation. Healthcare networks, energy operators and government agencies in Kern County typically choose the combination of on-site options and certified off-site processing that best meets their compliance needs."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What industries do you serve in Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS serves the primary industries of Kern County including energy and oilfield operations, industrial agriculture, healthcare networks, K-12 and higher education institutions, and local government agencies. STS engagements with these sectors typically include secure logistics, documented data destruction, compliance reporting and zero-landfill processing tailored to each vertical’s regulatory requirements."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How quickly can you schedule pickup in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS typically provides same-week scheduling for Bakersfield and Kern County clients. Energy operators, healthcare facilities and school districts often require coordination around operational hours or academic calendars. Early contact allows our team to reserve the earliest available slot that meets your project timeline while maintaining full chain of custody documentation from pickup through final processing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide certificates of destruction?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Every engagement includes a certificate of destruction that lists serial numbers, destruction method, weight and downstream tracking. These certificates support audit requirements for HIPAA, NIST 800-88, GLBA and other regulatory frameworks. Certificates are delivered promptly after processing is completed at our certified facilities in Jacksonville, Texas and Houston, Texas."
          }
        }
